WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Start with why.

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:05.087
Most federal estates still run
the client/server model they

3
00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:09.087
built in the early 2000s, with
Active Directory at the center.

4
00:00:09.087 --> 00:00:12.413
And the directory has been doing
more than anyone wrote down.

5
00:00:12.413 --> 00:00:17.925
Putting a user or a computer in an organizational
unit, an organizational unit (OU),

6
00:00:17.925 --> 00:00:21.958
quietly decided several things
at once: who administers it,

7
00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:26.319
which Group Policy applies, what it
can reach, how it's named in DNS,

8
00:00:26.319 --> 00:00:29.775
and whether it's trusted
through its certificates.

9
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:30.987
None of that was wrong.

10
00:00:30.987 --> 00:00:35.376
It just was never recorded anywhere
else, and the cloud doesn't inherit it.

11
00:00:35.376 --> 00:00:38.708
Entra ID's administrative
units can't be nested,

12
00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:41.700
and policy follows groups, not containers.

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.618
So an agency that moves the users
and retires the forest without

14
00:00:45.618 --> 00:00:49.463
recovering those decisions isn't
modernizing its governance.

15
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:50.587
It's deleting it.

16
00:00:50.587 --> 00:00:52.730
The second reason is the calendar.
